# Bounded semantic preflight, not a codec or specialization implementation.
# Field/variant walk is mechanically adapted from all 97 hc_enc_* owners in
# compiler/20.hir/generated/hir_codec.spl; no decoder or encoded output is used.
# Frozen input SHA256: e6ddcf4358668819c508742ceb120372cabd3cb03b961a6584a80d0ca6780e05
# The 97 mono_pf_* names preserve the encoder suffix exactly. Every visited
# field, enum arm and optional branch corresponds to that source. Wire writes
# become resource reservations, array lengths reserve before loops, dictionary
# snapshots reserve a concrete typed count first, sorting is unnecessary here.
# Reconcile this mirror when the exported codec/schema versions change; the
# public entries refuse differing actual versions/rules before visiting HIR.
# Unknown enum variants fail closed. No canonical-codec availability is claimed.
#
# Allocation-free dictionary cardinality uses the existing typed provider:
# _MirLoweringExpr/method_calls_literals.spl routes HirTypeKind.Dict .len()
# to rt_dict_len; runtime_native.c reads the same registered dictionary length
# used by rt_dict_keys. The pure-Simple core_array provider uses dict_len_value
# for the same pair. These concrete receiver types prevent erased rt_len.
# Snapshot equality detects inconsistency; it is not a substitute for the
# provider's count/keys contract, and native qualification remains UNRUN.
